        "noSubjects": "No obstacles yet.",
        "gmNotes": "<p><strong>Example: Chase, Run Away.</strong> The PCs flee. Built for four level-3 PCs: base DC 18, easy 16. Six obstacles.</p><p>The cult's guards set the granary alight behind the party and give chase. The PCs act first; the guards act second. Rounds are about a minute.</p><p><strong>Each roll:</strong> a success earns 1 Chase Point, a critical success 2, and a critical failure loses 1. Use + and − on the obstacle. When it is full, mark it Complete, add 1 to Party and reveal the next obstacle. Chase Points don't carry over.</p><p><strong>The guards</strong> start one obstacle behind and move 1 each round on Next round.</p><p><strong>It ends</strong> when Party gets past obstacle 6 to the river ferry, or Party is 3 obstacles ahead at the end of a round (the guards give up). If the Guards reach Party's obstacle, run a combat.</p>",
